The Dust Storm
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/relay_post]

FIXME(mundane): You are on the mesa road when the storm comes up out of the south. The light goes wrong first, then the air, then everything. Visibility collapses to arm's-length. Grit drives into exposed skin and works under your collar. The sky turns the color of rust.

FIXME(mundane): There is no shelter on this stretch of road. Flat rock, scrub brush, the bones of an old fence. You cast around for anything and almost miss it: a low stone building set against the slope, a Kesharat pennant snapping on a pole, the whole structure barely a shape inside the murk.

choices:

* Make for the building = Push toward the Kesharat post
    FIXME(mundane): You put your shoulder to the wind and cross the open ground at a run. The door is unlatched. You shove it open against the storm and fall inside in a wash of grit and noise. A woman at a desk gets up and crosses to the door, puts her shoulder against it, and forces the latch closed. She turns to you. She is delighted to see you.
    FIXME(mundane): Her name is Devra. She is mid-thirties. She is sharp-featured. She has ink on her fingers. She is the relay operator. She has been here four years. She is alone at the post tonight. She is glad of the company and talks too much.
    FIXME(mundane): She sits you down at a stool by the brazier and gives you tea from her own teapot. She offers you a place to wait out the storm. She asks about the road south, the towns you have passed through, the news from anywhere. You have been a person on a road for a day. To her you are the whole world coming in out of the dust.
    FIXME(dread): After a while she stops asking. She fetches her work log down off the desk and brings it over to the brazier and shows it to you. The log is a private notebook. It is not the official file. It is her own annotation of the wire messages she has been transcribing lately. She says she wants someone outside the system to look at them with her. She apologizes for the imposition and then does not stop.
    FIXME(dread): She shows you the original transcriptions in the official file: each one is a sheet of carbon paper carrying the standard wire header from the regional office. They look correct in every procedural way. Then she walks you through the strange ones. An order to construct a resonance platform at coordinates that match empty desert. A request for four hundred units of aligned calcium, a material no catalog lists. A personnel transfer for an ID that does not match any known format. She files them all because that is her job. She does not know what to do about them.
    +add_tag relay_post.met_devra
    +add_tag relay_post.saw_wire
    FIXME(mundane): A heavy knock at the back door cuts her off. She freezes. Then she gets up, crosses the room, and works the bolt. An old man comes in, shaking dust from a heavy oilskin. Devra stiffens. The old man takes off his coat and hangs it on a peg without comment. He looks at you, looks at her, and crosses to the brazier for the tea.
    +open "The Relay Post"

* Ride it out in place = Find a hollow and wait the storm out
    You wedge yourself behind a slab of caprock and pull your cloak across your face. The wind takes hours to ease. When it does the post is still there across the flat, a stone shape in the settling dust, but the urgency is gone and so is your reason to knock.
    +flee_dungeon
